{
  "summary": "Built a new, self-contained Rowad Alfa Auto Care marketing site under 'Rowad Alfa_AI Agent/' (Vite+React+TS+Tailwind+Framer Motion+React Router), per the user's explicit choice to nest it inside this repo. Researched the business via logged-out browsing of instagram.com/rowad_alfa_auto_care (name, tagline, categories, brands, an offer, address, phone numbers; stopped once Instagram required login rather than attempting to bypass it). Wrote ROWAD_ALFA_PRODUCT_DESIGN_PLAN.md, then implemented the full information architecture: Home (scrolling profile), Services (+detail), Products (+category+detail with related items), Offers, Gallery (original SVG/gradient visual concepts, no Instagram images reused), Social (content library + weekly planner with a working platform filter), Contact. All business facts are tagged observed-vs-inferred in the UI itself; no fabricated stats/certifications/ratings.",
  "nextSteps": "This is additive, untracked content inside the WhatsApp AI Agent repo (git status will show it as untracked) — no commit was made since none was requested. If the user wants it committed/pushed later, treat it as a separate concern from the WhatsApp agent's own history. Genuine remaining work: real product photography/specs from the business itself (current data is originally-authored, business-consistent placeholder content, not live inventory), and no backend exists yet for the content planner (it's a client-side preview only).",
  "tests": "npm run typecheck, npm run lint, and npm run build all pass clean in Rowad Alfa_AI Agent/. Live browser QA: every route (/, /services, /services/:slug, /products, /products/:category, /products/:category/:slug, /offers, /gallery, /social, /contact, and an unknown route for 404) verified with zero console errors. Two real UI bugs found and fixed during QA: (1) low-contrast hero heading against the background art on mobile, fixed with a scrim overlay and white heading text; (2) the weekly-planner table used a fixed desktop grid that overflowed on mobile instead of reflowing, fixed with a responsive card layout below the md breakpoint. Docker was not attempted — this sub-project has no Dockerfile and none was requested.",
  "lastHandoff": "handoffs/1064caee-f2bf-45b5-b4ed-9f47ff7a7810-2caf3737-96cc-4128-86a5-5e3279d5e465.json",
